The registered Google callback is the apex (aapawz.com) but the platform
308-redirects apex→www, so every OAuth flow that starts on one host
finishes on the other. Host-only pawz_oauth_b / pawz_session cookies were
invisible after the hop: the browser-binding guard failed and the callback
silently bounced the owner back to the login page AFTER authorization
(oauth_states row 11:53Z consumed, no google_sub linked).

- cookieDomainForHost()/requestHost() in pawz-auth: on aapawz.com hosts
  auth cookies now carry Domain=.aapawz.com (shared apex+www); host-only
  everywhere else (localhost/previews).
- Wired into google initiator (binding cookie), callback (session),
  login, email-link (session), and logout (clears BOTH variants).
